[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3188148815","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/109607#issuecomment-3188148815","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/109607","id":3188148815,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6-B0pP","user":{"login":"rburing","id":229837,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyOTgzNw==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/229837?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rburing","html_url":"https://github.com/rburing","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rburing/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rburing/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rburing/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rburing/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rburing/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rburing/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rburing/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rburing/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rburing/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-08-14T11:41:06Z","updated_at":"2025-08-14T11:41:06Z","body":"The instance is not always guaranteed to be a `CollisionObject*D`, e.g. with tile maps, grid maps, CSG, or manual use of the physics server. I agree we should get rid of the sync somehow though.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3188148815/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3188203105","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/109607#issuecomment-3188203105","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/109607","id":3188203105,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6-CB5h","user":{"login":"mihe","id":4884246,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ4ODQyNDY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4884246?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe","html_url":"https://github.com/mihe","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-08-14T12:01:21Z","updated_at":"2025-08-14T12:05:40Z","body":"> The instance is not always guaranteed to be a `CollisionObject*D`, e.g. with tile maps, grid maps, CSG, or manual use of the physics server. I agree we should get rid of the sync somehow though.\r\n\r\nRight, good point. I guess there's technically `SoftBody3D` as well, but I'm not sure if those are relevant for floor/wall collisions, or even hit by `body_test_motion` at all.\r\n\r\nAnyway, that's very annoying, and a bit of a showstopper.\r\n\r\nThere's gotta be something else we can do to avoid this, other than tacking on more arbitrary data in `MotionResult` or `PhysicsDirectBodyState*D`.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3188203105/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3188333550","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/109607#issuecomment-3188333550","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/109607","id":3188333550,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6-Chvu","user":{"login":"mihe","id":4884246,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ4ODQyNDY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4884246?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe","html_url":"https://github.com/mihe","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-08-14T12:47:25Z","updated_at":"2025-08-14T12:48:54Z","body":"The manual use of the physics server use-case really kills pretty much anything other than `MotionResult` or `PhysicsDirectBodyState*D` though.\r\n\r\nAdding another getter to `PhysicsDirectBodyState*D` is arguably the lesser evil of the two, but I'm not super happy about that, as that class has until now largely just been about `_integrate_forces` stuff, and collision layer/mask doesn't feel very force integration-y.\r\n\r\nIt's not the end of the world though, I guess, and while it sets a questionable precedent, I don't think it's worth keeping this synchronization around to avoid it, so I'll go ahead and just do it.\r\n\r\nThe concern you (@rburing) had [here](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/94205#issuecomment-2227314490) about the `!Thread::is_main_thread()` check is presumably moot anyway, since we've been calling `body_get_direct_state` from `move_and_slide` for years now. The only place I see that being a real problem is if you use the thread groups feature, but we have plenty of other nodes that break with that (e.g. `RayCast*D`, `ShapeCast*D`).","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3188333550/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3188479438","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/109607#issuecomment-3188479438","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/109607","id":3188479438,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6-DFXO","user":{"login":"mihe","id":4884246,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ4ODQyNDY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4884246?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe","html_url":"https://github.com/mihe","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-08-14T13:33:43Z","updated_at":"2025-08-14T13:38:38Z","body":"There, the collision layer and mask are now exposed through `PhysicsDirectBodyState*D` and `move_and_slide` makes use of those getters instead of going through `PhysicsServer*D`.\r\n\r\nI'd appreciate a review, if/when you can find the time, @rburing.\r\n\r\nKeep in mind that using `PhysicsDirectBodyState*D` in `move_and_slide` is not strictly thread-safe as-is, and should ideally be merged along with #109591, but the call to `get_velocity_at_local_position` in `move_and_slide` is already suffering from this same problem, so we're not making things any worse really.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3188479438/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3188642245","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/109607#issuecomment-3188642245","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/109607","id":3188642245,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6-DtHF","user":{"login":"rburing","id":229837,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyOTgzNw==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/229837?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rburing","html_url":"https://github.com/rburing","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rburing/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rburing/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rburing/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rburing/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rburing/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rburing/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rburing/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rburing/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rburing/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-08-14T14:22:40Z","updated_at":"2025-08-14T14:22:40Z","body":"Since current GDExtension physics servers don't implement this (yet) on their direct body state, can we expose the property and then add GDExtension compatibility methods that fall back to syncing with `body_get_collision_layer`?","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3188642245/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3188935077","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/109607#issuecomment-3188935077","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/109607","id":3188935077,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6-E0ml","user":{"login":"mihe","id":4884246,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ4ODQyNDY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4884246?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe","html_url":"https://github.com/mihe","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-08-14T15:46:37Z","updated_at":"2025-08-14T15:54:34Z","body":"> can we expose the property and then add GDExtension compatibility methods that fall back to syncing with `body_get_collision_layer`?\r\n\r\nI was just about to say that none of the other methods are properties, but I had of course completely forgot that most of them are in fact bound as properties through `_bind_methods`, so that needed to be done either way.\r\n\r\nThat would presumably mean that we also need to invoke the getter as a property, meaning we'd be calling `Object::get`? That seems a little bit off to me.\r\n\r\nThere is another way of achieving the same thing, which is to not use the `EXBIND*` macros in `PhysicsDirectBodyState*DExtension` and just do the `GDVIRTUAL` declarations manually, along with a `GDVIRTUAL_IS_OVERRIDDEN` check that falls back on `PhysicsServer*D::body_get_collision_layer`. That could then be compiled out with `DISABLE_DEPRECATED` in favor of the normal `EXBIND*` stuff.\r\n\r\nBoth would be a bit odd-looking, but maybe the latter is preferable?","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3188935077/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3189082897","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/109607#issuecomment-3189082897","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/109607","id":3189082897,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6-FYsR","user":{"login":"rburing","id":229837,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyOTgzNw==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/229837?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rburing","html_url":"https://github.com/rburing","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rburing/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rburing/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rburing/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rburing/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rburing/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rburing/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rburing/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rburing/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rburing/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-08-14T16:29:35Z","updated_at":"2025-08-14T16:29:35Z","body":"+1 for the latter, sounds fine to me. I'll approve afterward.\r\n\r\nYou could add me as coauthor if you want, but no big deal either way.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3189082897/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3189086254","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/109607#issuecomment-3189086254","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/109607","id":3189086254,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6-FZgu","user":{"login":"mihe","id":4884246,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ4ODQyNDY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4884246?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe","html_url":"https://github.com/mihe","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-08-14T16:30:39Z","updated_at":"2025-08-14T16:34:20Z","body":"I pushed the method/property bindings.\r\n\r\nHowever, it seems there's a bigger problem with this GDExtension compatibility stuff, which is that we don't have the `RID` for the body whose `PhysicsDirectBodyState*D` we're dealing with, in something like `PhysicsDirectBodyState*DExtension`, which we need to call `PhysicsServer*D::body_get_collision_layer`. So whatever \"dynamic dispatch\" we'd want to do would need to happen inside of `CharacterBody*D::_set_platform_data`, where we actually have the `RID`.\r\n\r\nI'm not sure if it's actually possible from outside the class to check whether that particular instance of `PhysicsDirectBodyState*D` has overridden a particular method.\r\n\r\nEDIT: Added you as co-author.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3189086254/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3189188455","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/109607#issuecomment-3189188455","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/109607","id":3189188455,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6-Fydn","user":{"login":"rburing","id":229837,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyOTgzNw==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/229837?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rburing","html_url":"https://github.com/rburing","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rburing/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rburing/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rburing/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rburing/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rburing/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rburing/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rburing/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rburing/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rburing/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-08-14T16:57:47Z","updated_at":"2025-08-14T16:57:47Z","body":"Ah, right. I think (if not `DISABLE_DEPRECATED`) we could cast to `PhysicsDirectBodyState3DExtension` and use the `GDVIRTUAL_IS_OVERRIDDEN_PTR` macro to check for an overridden method from outside. It becomes a bit cursed-looking though.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3189188455/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3189195404","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/109607#issuecomment-3189195404","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/109607","id":3189195404,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6-F0KM","user":{"login":"mihe","id":4884246,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ4ODQyNDY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4884246?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe","html_url":"https://github.com/mihe","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-08-14T17:00:16Z","updated_at":"2025-08-14T17:00:16Z","body":"> I think (if not `DISABLE_DEPRECATED`) we could cast to `PhysicsDirectBodyState3DExtension` and use the `GDVIRTUAL_IS_OVERRIDDEN_PTR` macro to check for an overridden method from outside. It becomes a bit cursed-looking though.\r\n\r\nI was just in the middle of pushing this exact thing. 😅\r\n\r\nBut yeah, I'm not a fan, especially with needing to involve `PhysicsDirectBodyState*DExtension` in `CharacterBody*D`.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3189195404/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3192330291","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/109607#issuecomment-3192330291","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/109607","id":3192330291,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6-Rxgz","user":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-08-15T18:04:48Z","updated_at":"2025-08-15T18:04:48Z","body":"Thanks! ","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3192330291/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]